{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-EIP7951-POSTCOND-001-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-EIP7951-POSTCOND-001-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7951-POSTCOND-001", "graph_element_under_test": "STATE-PRECOMPILE-COMPLETE", "title": "Falsify secp256r1 precompile return value format consistency across execution paths", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["Transaction"], "attacker_controlled": true, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Consensus Divergence", "risk_category": "State Transition", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Deploy a contract that calls the secp256r1 precompile (0x0b / address TBD per EIP-7951) with a valid signature and checks returndata size == 32 and returndata == 0x0000...0001. 2. Deploy a second contract that calls with invalid signature (wrong r, s, or public key) and checks returndata size == 0. 3. Execute both transactions in a block and verify all client implementations produce identical return values. 4. Edge cases: (a) valid signature but point-at-infinity public key, (b) signature with s > n/2 (malleability), (c) zero-length input, (d) input shorter than 160 bytes. 5. Compare return values across at least two EL client implementations.", "executable_checks": ["Create test transaction calling precompile with valid (r, s, x, y, hash) and assert returndata == bytes32(1)", "Create test transaction calling precompile with invalid signature and assert returndata == bytes(0)", "Fuzz input lengths from 0 to 200 bytes and verify consistent return across clients"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-EIP7951-POSTCOND-001. Post-condition check. Divergent return formats across clients would cause consensus split on any block containing a secp256r1 precompile call. Covers nodes: ACTION-RETURN-SUCCESS, ACTION-RETURN-EMPTY, STATE-PRECOMPILE-COMPLETE."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7951-POSTCOND-001", "subg