{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-FULUFC-PRECOND-002-BOUNDARY", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-FULUFC-PRECOND-002-BOUNDARY", "property_id": "PROP-W0-FULUFC-PRECOND-002", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-CHECK-SLOT-NOT-FUTURE", "title": "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for future-slot block rejection in fork choice", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["P2P"], "attacker_controlled": true, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Input Validation Bypass", "risk_category": "Fork Choice", "severity_hint": "MEDIUM", "detection_procedure": "1. Construct a signed beacon block with slot = get_current_slot(store) + 1 (one slot in the future). 2. Send this block via P2P gossip to a target node. 3. Verify the block is rejected by the fork choice store (on_block should fail the slot check). 4. Test boundary: slot exactly equal to current slot (should be accepted). 5. Test slot = current_slot + SECONDS_PER_SLOT (edge of tolerance). 6. Verify no state mutation occurs when the future block is rejected.", "executable_checks": ["Send block with slot = current_slot + 1 via P2P and verify rejection", "Send block with slot = current_slot and verify acceptance (if otherwise valid)", "Verify store state is unchanged after future block rejection"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-FULUFC-PRECOND-002. Boundary property. Covers edges: EDGE-PARENT-OK-TO-SLOT, EDGE-SLOT-FAIL. An attacker sending future-dated blocks via P2P could manipulate fork choice if the slot check is bypassed."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W0-FULUFC-PRECOND-002", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-FULU-FC-VALIDATION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_5db2f74bcc0c_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-FULU-FC-VALIDATION", "aspect": "validation", "title": "Fulu Fork Choice: Block Validation Pipeline", "description": "Models the sequential validation checks performed on an incoming block before it i