{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-FULUFC-INV-001-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W0-FULUFC-INV-001-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W0-FULUFC-INV-001", "graph_element_under_test": "STATE-PARENT-STATE-COPIED", "title": "Falsify deep copy isolation between parent and child beacon states", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "State Corruption", "risk_category": "State Transition", "severity_hint": "HIGH", "detection_procedure": "1. Obtain a reference to the parent beacon state from the fork choice store. 2. Execute on_block which copies the parent state and applies state_transition. 3. After state_transition completes, compare the parent state in the store with a snapshot taken before the operation. 4. Specifically check mutable nested structures: (a) validator registry entries, (b) balances array, (c) slashings array, (d) participation flags, (e) proposer_lookahead array (new in Fulu). 5. Modify the child state and verify parent state is unaffected. 6. Language-specific: check for reference sharing in Python (id() comparison), Go (pointer comparison), Rust (Rc/Arc sharing).", "executable_checks": ["Snapshot parent state hash before on_block, verify unchanged after", "Mutate child state validator balance, verify parent validator balance unchanged", "Check proposer_lookahead array in child vs parent for reference independence"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-FULUFC-INV-001. Invariant falsification. Covers nodes: STATE-PARENT-STATE-COPIED, ACTION-STATE-TRANSITION-EXEC. Shallow copy bug would corrupt the fork choice store across blocks, affecting all subsequent fork choice decisions."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W0-FULUFC-INV-001", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-FULU-FC-STATE-TRANSITION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_5db2f74bcc0c_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {