{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W1-DASCORE-INV-005-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W1-DASCORE-INV-005-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W1-DASCORE-INV-005", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-EXPOSE-RECONSTRUCTED", "title": "Falsify equivalence of reconstructed and gossip-received column handling", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Logic Error", "risk_category": "Data Availability Sampling (PeerDAS)", "severity_hint": "MEDIUM", "detection_procedure": "1. Obtain a set of data columns via gossip for a known block. 2. Independently reconstruct the same columns from sufficient erasure-coded pieces. 3. Compare the internal representation: (a) data content must be byte-identical, (b) metadata (block_root, column_index, slot) must match, (c) KZG proofs must be identical. 4. Verify both gossip-received and reconstructed columns pass the same validation pipeline. 5. Check if any internal flags or status fields differentiate reconstructed from received columns (they should not for downstream processing).", "executable_checks": ["Reconstruct columns and compare byte-for-byte with gossip-received equivalents", "Verify reconstructed columns pass the same is_data_available check", "Check internal data structures for any differentiation between sources"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W1-DASCORE-INV-005. Invariant falsification. Related ambiguity: AMB-DAS-CORE-04. Inconsistent treatment could cause DA sampling failures."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W1-DASCORE-INV-005", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-DAS-CORE-RECONSTRUCTION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_170b68e3c9a7_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-DAS-CORE-RECONSTRUCTION", "aspect": "state_transition", "title": "DAS Core: Matrix Reconstruction and Cross-Seeding", "description": "Models the erasure coding r