{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W1-EIP7607-POSTCOND-001-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W1-EIP7607-POSTCOND-001-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W1-EIP7607-POSTCOND-001", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-UPDATE-FORK-ID", "title": "Falsify Fusaka fork identifier correctness after activation", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Configuration Error", "risk_category": "P2P Network", "severity_hint": "HIGH", "detection_procedure": "1. Set up a node configured for Fusaka fork at a specific epoch. 2. Advance the node past the fork epoch. 3. Query the node's fork_id (via devp2p Status message or internal API). 4. Verify the fork_id matches the expected value: CRC32 of genesis hash XOR'd with fork block number/timestamp. 5. For mainnet: verify fork_id == 0x5167e2a6 (or whatever the final value is). 6. Cross-check: connect two nodes post-fork and verify they successfully peer (matching fork_ids). 7. Cross-check: connect a pre-fork and post-fork node and verify they reject each other.", "executable_checks": ["Verify fork_id value matches specification after fork activation", "Verify two post-fork nodes can peer successfully", "Verify pre-fork and post-fork nodes reject peering"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W1-EIP7607-POSTCOND-001. Post-condition falsification. Wrong fork ID would isolate nodes on the network. Covers nodes: ACTION-UPDATE-FORK-ID, STATE-FUSAKA-ACTIVE."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W1-EIP7607-POSTCOND-001", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7607-FORK-ACTIVATION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_6c2d513ce6d6866d954a4c47899423e02637fdef.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7607-FORK-ACTIVATION", "aspect": "consensus", "title": "EIP-7607: Fusaka Network Upgrade Activation", "description": "Models the coordinated activation of Fusaka/Osaka network upgrade 