{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W3-EIP7918-RESERVE-INV-003-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W3-EIP7918-RESERVE-INV-003-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W3-EIP7918-RESERVE-INV-003", "graph_element_under_test": "CONST-BLOB-BASE-COST", "title": "Falsify EIP-7918 constant values (BLOB_BASE_COST and GAS_PER_BLOB)", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Incorrect Constant", "risk_category": "State Transition", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. In each EL client implementation, locate the BLOB_BASE_COST constant definition. 2. Verify BLOB_BASE_COST == 8192 (2^13). 3. Locate GAS_PER_BLOB constant. Verify GAS_PER_BLOB == 131072 (2^17). 4. Compute the ratio: BLOB_BASE_COST / GAS_PER_BLOB. Verify it equals 1/16. 5. Cross-check across all EL client implementations (Geth, Nethermind, Besu, Reth, Erigon). 6. Verify no integer overflow in reserve price calculation: BLOB_BASE_COST * base_fee_per_gas (could overflow uint64 at high base fees).", "executable_checks": ["Verify BLOB_BASE_COST == 8192 in each client", "Verify GAS_PER_BLOB == 131072 in each client", "Check for integer overflow in BLOB_BASE_COST * max_possible_base_fee_per_gas"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W3-EIP7918-RESERVE-INV-003. Invariant falsification. Wrong constants would affect every block's fee calculation, causing immediate consensus split."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W3-EIP7918-RESERVE-INV-003", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7918-RESERVE-PRICE", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_c3ce7ae8484274a9b81bd1c5073ce548c23817ee.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7918-RESERVE-PRICE", "aspect": "gas_economics", "title": "EIP-7918: Blob Base Fee Reserve Price Mechanism", "description": "Models the reserve price floor that prevents blob base fee from falling below a ratio of execution costs",