{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W5-EIP7823-VAL-PRECOND-003-BOUNDARY", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W5-EIP7823-VAL-PRECOND-003-BOUNDARY", "property_id": "PROP-W5-EIP7823-VAL-PRECOND-003", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-CHECK-MODULUS-LENGTH", "title": "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for MODEXP modulus length upper bound enforcement", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["Transaction"], "attacker_controlled": true, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Input Validation Bypass", "risk_category": "Block Validation", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Submit a transaction calling MODEXP precompile (address 0x05) with modulus_length = 1025 bytes (one over the 1024 limit). 2. Verify the precompile returns empty (rejects) before performing any computation. 3. Test with modulus_length = 1024 (should succeed). 4. Test with modulus_length = 0 (edge case). 5. Test with modulus_length = 2^32 - 1 (max uint32, if length is 32-bit). 6. Measure execution time for modulus_length = 1024 vs 1025: the 1025 case must return instantly (no computation). 7. Test all three input lengths (base, exponent, modulus) against their respective bounds.", "executable_checks": ["Submit MODEXP with modulus_length = 1025, verify immediate rejection", "Submit MODEXP with modulus_length = 1024, verify success", "Measure execution time: 1025 must be near-zero (no computation)"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W5-EIP7823-VAL-PRECOND-003. Boundary property. Trust boundary: attacker-controlled calldata via on-chain transaction. Unbounded modulus causes excessive computation potentially crashing all clients."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W5-EIP7823-VAL-PRECOND-003", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7823-VALIDATION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_a86b199c00c1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7823-VALIDATION", "aspect": "validation", "title": "EIP-7823: MODEXP In