{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W6-FULU-FORK-ST-PRECOND-002-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W6-FULU-FORK-ST-PRECOND-002-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W6-FULU-FORK-ST-PRECOND-002", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-CHECK-FORK-EPOCH", "title": "Falsify fork upgrade application during state replay at FULU_FORK_EPOCH boundary", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "State Divergence", "risk_category": "State Transition", "severity_hint": "HIGH", "detection_procedure": "1. Start a node from a pre-fork checkpoint state. 2. Replay blocks through the FULU_FORK_EPOCH boundary. 3. Verify upgrade_to_fulu is called at exactly the correct slot (FULU_FORK_EPOCH * SLOTS_PER_EPOCH). 4. Verify the upgrade is applied regardless of syncing mode (full sync, checkpoint sync, optimistic sync). 5. Compare post-upgrade state root with a reference node that was live during the fork. 6. Test: skip the fork epoch slot entirely (empty slot). Verify the upgrade still applies at the epoch boundary.", "executable_checks": ["Replay through fork epoch, verify upgrade_to_fulu is called at correct slot", "Test with empty slot at fork epoch, verify upgrade still applies", "Compare post-upgrade state root with reference"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W6-FULU-FORK-ST-PRECOND-002. Pre-condition falsification. Related ambiguity: AMB-FULU-FORK-01. Nodes that skip the fork during sync would fork off the main chain."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W6-FULU-FORK-ST-PRECOND-002", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-FULU-FORK-STATE-TRANSITION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_48e6b04749aa_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-FULU-FORK-STATE-TRANSITION", "aspect": "state_transition", "title": "Fulu Fork: Beacon State Upgrade Transition", "description": "Models the state migration from Electra to Fulu c