{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W6-EIP7927-ACT-INV-002-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W6-EIP7927-ACT-INV-002-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W6-EIP7927-ACT-INV-002", "graph_element_under_test": "STATE-DEPOSIT-LOGS-PROCESSED", "title": "Falsify EIP-6110 implementation completeness before history expiry activation", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Dependency Violation", "risk_category": "Consensus Logic", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Verify the CL client processes deposits via EIP-6110 (in-protocol deposits from execution layer) rather than reading deposit contract logs from historical EL data. 2. After history expiry: attempt to process a new validator deposit. Verify it succeeds via EIP-6110. 3. Verify the CL does NOT attempt to read historical deposit contract logs (which would fail after history expiry). 4. Check for any code paths that still reference the deposit contract log method. 5. Test: process a deposit after the EL has pruned pre-merge history.", "executable_checks": ["Process validator deposit after history expiry, verify success via EIP-6110", "Verify no code path reads deposit contract logs post-history-expiry", "Code audit: search for legacy deposit log reading code"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W6-EIP7927-ACT-INV-002. Invariant falsification. Related assumption: ASSUM-EIP7927-03. Missing EIP-6110 implementation combined with history expiry would halt all new validator activations."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W6-EIP7927-ACT-INV-002", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7927-HISTORY-EXPIRY", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_d381b878f342.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7927-HISTORY-EXPIRY", "aspect": "state_transition", "title": "EIP-7927: Pre-Merge History Expiry Lifecycle", "description": "Models the state t