{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-EIP7935-SECBND-INV-001-BOUNDARY", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-EIP7935-SECBND-INV-001-BOUNDARY", "property_id": "PROP-W7-EIP7935-SECBND-INV-001", "graph_element_under_test": "STATE-WORST-CASE-BLOCK-SIZE", "title": "Verify Trust Boundary Integrity for worst-case block size within 10 MiB gossip limit at 60M gas", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["P2P"], "attacker_controlled": true, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Resource Exhaustion", "risk_category": "Block Validation", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Construct an adversarial block maximizing serialized size within 60M gas: (a) maximum calldata (16 gas/byte non-zero, 4 gas/byte zero), (b) maximum contract creation initcode, (c) maximum LOG operations with data, (d) maximum RETURN data. 2. Measure the RLP-serialized size of the block. 3. Verify it is strictly < 10 MiB. 4. Try novel constructions: combine multiple size-maximizing strategies. 5. Account for: block header, transaction list overhead, uncle/ommers (should be empty post-merge). 6. If a construction exceeds 10 MiB, this is a critical finding: CL would reject valid EL blocks.", "executable_checks": ["Construct max-calldata block at 60M gas, measure serialized size", "Construct max-LOG-data block at 60M gas, measure serialized size", "Verify all constructions produce size < 10 MiB"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W7-EIP7935-SECBND-INV-001. Boundary property. Related assumption: ASSUM-EIP7935-03. If violated, attacker produces valid EL blocks that CL rejects, causing consensus-execution layer split affecting all nodes. Requires PoC: construct a block within 60M gas whose serialized size >= 10 MiB."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W7-EIP7935-SECBND-INV-001", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7935-SECURITY-BOUNDARY", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_4ecc6b6b38e1a1883b5fefd1dc59191bc25b02d9_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7935-SECURITY-BOUNDARY", "aspect": "security_boundary", "title": "EIP-7935: Worst-Case Block Size and Consensus Gossip Limits", "description": "Models the security boundary between block gas capacity and consensus layer gossip limits, ensuring adversarial blocks stay within safe bounds", "nodes": [{"id": "STATE-BLOCK-GAS-60M", "label": "Block Gas Limit at 60M", "type": "State", "description": "Block can contain up to 60M gas worth of transactions"}, {"id": "ACTION-ADVERSARIAL-BLOCK-CONSTRUCTION", "label": "Adversarial Block Construction", "type": "Action", "description": "Attacker constructs a block that maximizes serialized size (e.g., using zero-byte-heavy calldata) to approach worst-case block size", "precondition": ["STATE-BLOCK-GAS-60M"], "postcondition": ["STATE-WORST-CASE-BLOCK-SIZE"]}, {"id": "STATE-WORST-CASE-BLOCK-SIZE", "label": "Worst-Case Block Size Computed", "type": "State", "description": "The maximum possible serialized block size under 60M gas, which must remain below CL gossip limits"}, {"id": "ACTION-CL-GOSSIP-VALIDATION", "label": "CL Validates Block Against Gossip Limit", "type": "Action", "description": "Consensus layer checks that incoming block does not exceed the 10 MiB gossip message size limit", "precondition": ["STATE-WORST-CASE-BLOCK-SIZE"], "postcondition": ["STATE-BLOCK-WITHIN-GOSSIP-LIMIT", "STATE-BLOCK-EXCEEDS-GOSSIP-LIMIT"]}, {"id": "STATE-BLOCK-WITHIN-GOSSIP-LIMIT", "label": "Block Within 10 MiB Gossip Limit", "type": "State", "description": "Block size is within CL gossip limits and can propagate through the P2P network"}, {"id": "STATE-BLOCK-EXCEEDS-GOSSIP-LIMIT", "label": "Block Exceeds Gossip Limit", "type": "State", "description": "Block size exceeds CL gossip limit, would fail to propagate (should not occur below 150M gas)"}], "edges": [{"id": "EDGE-ATTACKER-CONSTRUCTS", "source": "STATE-BLOCK-GAS-60M", "target": "ACTION-ADVERSARIAL-BLOCK-CONSTRUCTION", "label": "