{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-PCS-VERIFY-INV-001-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-PCS-VERIFY-INV-001-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W7-PCS-VERIFY-INV-001", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-COMPUTE-FIAT-SHAMIR-CHALLENGE", "title": "Falsify Fiat-Shamir challenge determinism and collision resistance in batch verification", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["P2P"], "attacker_controlled": true, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Cryptographic Weakness", "risk_category": "Data Availability Sampling (PeerDAS)", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Compute the Fiat-Shamir challenge r for a batch verification with specific (commitments, cell_indices, cells). 2. Modify one cell slightly and recompute r. Verify r changes. 3. Swap two commitments and recompute r. Verify r changes. 4. Test with duplicate commitments: verify they are included in the hash (not deduplicated). 5. Verify the hash domain separation includes all batch parameters. 6. Attempt to find two different inputs that produce the same challenge (collision search). 7. Verify the implementation matches the spec exactly (byte ordering, encoding).", "executable_checks": ["Compute r, modify one cell, verify r changes", "Test with duplicate commitments, verify they affect r", "Verify implementation matches spec byte-for-byte"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W7-PCS-VERIFY-INV-001. Invariant falsification. Related ambiguity: AMB-PCS-FULU-04. Fiat-Shamir weakness allows proof forgery, enabling invalid cells to pass batch verification across all nodes."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W7-PCS-VERIFY-INV-001", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-PCS-VALIDATION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_b9c308f06c06b2d7090db74d932d2555bce8e637_1770079940_1.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-PCS-VALIDATION", "aspect": "validation", "title": "Cell KZG Proof Batch Verification", "descr