{"check_id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-EIP7600-FORK-INV-002-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W5-PROP-W7-EIP7600-FORK-INV-002-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W7-EIP7600-FORK-INV-002", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-APPLY-PECTRA-TRANSITION", "title": "Falsify Prague-Electra simultaneous activation at the same slot/block boundary", "reachability": {"classification": "internal-only", "entry_points": ["Internal API"], "attacker_controlled": false, "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Activation Mismatch", "risk_category": "Consensus Logic", "severity_hint": "CRITICAL", "detection_procedure": "1. Verify the EL Prague activation timestamp and CL Electra activation epoch map to the same slot. 2. Compute: expected_el_timestamp = GENESIS_TIME + (ELECTRA_FORK_EPOCH * SLOTS_PER_EPOCH * SECONDS_PER_SLOT). 3. Verify the EL client's Prague activation timestamp matches this value. 4. Test: process a block at the activation boundary. Verify both EL and CL transitions apply to the same block. 5. Test: what happens if there's a missed slot at the activation boundary? Verify both layers still activate correctly. 6. Cross-check across all client pairs (EL+CL combinations).", "executable_checks": ["Verify EL Prague timestamp matches CL Electra epoch * SECONDS_PER_SLOT + GENESIS_TIME", "Process block at activation boundary, verify both layers transition", "Test missed slot at boundary, verify activation still occurs"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W7-EIP7600-FORK-INV-002. Invariant falsification. Related ambiguity: AMB-EIP7600-02. EL/CL fork activation mismatch would split the entire network."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W5_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W7-EIP7600-FORK-INV-002", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7600-FORK-ACTIVATION", "subgraph_file": "outputs/01b_SUBGRAPHS/spec_daa621eb522f.json", "subgraph": {"id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7600-FORK-ACTIVATION", "aspect": "consensus", "title": "EIP-7600: Pectra Fork Activation Lifecycle", "description": "Models