A-TRANSITION-COMPLETE", "source": "ACTION-APPLY-PECTRA-TRANSITION", "target": "STATE-POST-PECTRA", "label": "All Pectra fork rules applied"}], "external_entities": []}}
{"check_id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-001-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-001-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-001", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-CHARGE-GAS-6900", "title": "Falsify constant gas charge for secp256r1 precompile across all input paths", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["Transaction"], "attacker_controlled": true, "validation_layers": ["Transaction validation", "EVM execution"], "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Resource Exhaustion / Gas Metering Error", "risk_category": "Execution Layer - Precompile Gas Accounting", "severity_hint": "MEDIUM", "detection_procedure": "1. Deploy a contract that calls the secp256r1 precompile (address 0x100) with various inputs: (a) valid 160-byte input with correct signature, (b) valid 160-byte input with invalid signature, (c) empty input (0 bytes), (d) input shorter than 160 bytes, (e) input longer than 160 bytes. 2. For each call, measure exact gas consumed using gasleft() before and after the STATICCALL. 3. Verify that in ALL cases, exactly 6900 gas is deducted. 4. If any input path consumes different gas, the invariant is violated - attacker can spam cheap calls.", "executable_checks": ["Assert gasBefore - gasAfter == 6900 for valid signature verification", "Assert gasBefore - gasAfter == 6900 for invalid signature (wrong r,s values)", "Assert gasBefore - gasAfter == 6900 for malformed input (< 160 bytes)", "Assert gasBefore - gasAfter == 6900 for oversized input (> 160 bytes)", "Assert gasBefore - gasAfter == 6900 for empty input"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-001. Covers ACTION-CHARGE-GAS-6900, STATE-GAS-CHARGED. Invariant type - attempting falsification through diverse input paths. If gas is not charged for invalid inputs, attacker can spam precompile calls cheaply."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W6_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-001", "subgraph_i