{"check_id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7917-INV-003-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7917-INV-003-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7917-INV-003", "graph_element_under_test": "ACTION-GET-RANDAO-SEED", "title": "Falsify RANDAO seed epoch selection for proposer lookahead computation", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["Consensus Messages"], "attacker_controlled": false, "validation_layers": ["Epoch processing", "RANDAO mixing"], "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Cryptographic Weakness / Anti-Grinding Bypass", "risk_category": "Consensus Layer - Proposer Selection Security", "severity_hint": "HIGH", "detection_procedure": "1. In get_beacon_proposer_index or compute_proposer_index, verify the seed is retrieved via get_seed(state, epoch - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD - 1, DOMAIN_BEACON_PROPOSER). 2. Compare the epoch parameter: it must be N - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD - 1 (where N is the target epoch), NOT N - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD or N - 1. 3. Compute proposer schedules using both correct and incorrect seed epochs. 4. Verify that using epoch N - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD (off-by-one) produces different proposer assignments, confirming the seed epoch matters. 5. Verify the seed epoch predates any effective balance changes that could be manipulated.", "executable_checks": ["Assert seed epoch == target_epoch - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD - 1", "Assert proposer schedule differs when using wrong seed epoch (off-by-one test)", "Assert RANDAO mix at seed epoch was committed before effective balances for target epoch are known"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-EIP7917-INV-003. Invariant type. Related assumption ASSUM-EIP7917-01. Using wrong seed epoch weakens anti-grinding protection, allowing attackers to bias proposer selection via effective balance manipulation."}, "checklist_file": "outputs/02_CHECKLIST_PARTIAL_W6_1770089239_1.json", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7917-INV-003", "subgraph_id": "SUBGRAPH-EIP7917-LOOKAHEAD-COMPUTATION", "subgrap