{"check_id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-006-INTERNAL", "checklist_item": {"id": "CHECK-W6-PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-006-INTERNAL", "property_id": "PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-006", "graph_element_under_test": "STATE-ALL-VALIDATION-PASSED", "title": "Falsify secp256r1 validation ordering: attempt to skip intermediate checks", "reachability": {"classification": "external-reachable", "entry_points": ["Transaction"], "attacker_controlled": true, "validation_layers": ["Transaction validation", "EVM execution"], "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope"}, "bug_class": "Invalid Curve Attack / Validation Bypass", "risk_category": "Execution Layer - Cryptographic Precompile Security", "severity_hint": "HIGH", "detection_procedure": "1. Test each validation step in isolation: (a) Input < 160 bytes \u2192 must return empty (no further checks). (b) Input = 160 bytes but r >= curve_order \u2192 must return empty. (c) Input with s >= curve_order \u2192 must return empty. (d) Input with public key not on secp256r1 curve \u2192 must return empty. (e) Input with point at infinity as public key \u2192 must return empty. 2. For each case, verify the precompile does NOT reach the signature verification step. 3. Craft a point NOT on secp256r1 (invalid curve) and verify it's rejected before ECDSA verify. 4. Test with r=0, s=0, r=curve_order, s=curve_order as boundary values.", "executable_checks": ["Assert short input (< 160 bytes) returns empty without crash", "Assert r >= secp256r1_order returns empty", "Assert s >= secp256r1_order returns empty", "Assert point not on curve returns empty before verification", "Assert point at infinity returns empty", "Assert r=0, s=0 boundary cases handled correctly"], "notes": "Source: PROP-W0-EIP7951-INV-006. Invariant type - testing validation ordering. Skipping curve membership check before verification could enable invalid curve attacks. Covers full validation pipeline: length \u2192 sig bounds \u2192 pubkey bounds \u2192 curve \u2192 infinity."}, "checklist_file": "ou